---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import TrustBadge from "../components/TrustBadge.astro";
import SocialProof from "../components/SocialProof.astro";

const title = "ProForm Carbon Pro 9000 Review (2026): Specs and the Older 9000";
const description =
  "The ProForm Carbon Pro 9000 treadmill (PFTL16925): 16 in. screen, 3.6 CHP, 20 x 60 in. belt, 0-12% incline, 350 lb. How it differs from the older 22 in. Pro 9000, and who should buy it.";

const PRODUCTS = [
  {
    id: "proform-carbon-pro-9000",
    name: "ProForm Carbon Pro 9000",
    category: "ProForm’s Flagship Folding Treadmill",
    badge: "Current Model: PFTL16925",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FKTTWRZW?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$1,599-$1,799",
    priceBounds: {"low":1599,"high":1799},
    specs: "20 x 60 in. belt · 3.6 CHP · 0-12% incline · 0-12 mph · 350 lb max user · 16 in. HD touchscreen",
    pros: [
      "The largest screen and highest motor rating in ProForm’s current range",
      "A 350 lb rating, higher than NordicTrack’s T Series and the older Pro 9000",
      "A full 20 by 60-inch belt that folds with EasyLift assist",
      "Usually several hundred dollars less than NordicTrack machines with a similar screen",
    ],
    cons: [
      "No decline, unlike the older Pro 9000",
      "Two-year motor warranty on the flagship model",
      "Reviewers report a firm deck, some screen glare and slow incline changes",
      "Much of the console’s value depends on a paid iFIT membership",
    ],
    bottomLine: "A well-specified folding treadmill for walkers and moderate runners who want a big screen and a 350 lb rating — worth the premium over the Carbon Pro 2000 only if you will use the screen.",
    description: "The Carbon Pro 9000 (model PFTL16925) has a 20 by 60-inch belt with ProShox cushioning, a motor ProForm rates at 3.6 CHP, a speed range of 0 to 12 mph and incline from 0 to 12% with no decline. Maximum user weight is 350 lb. The 16-inch HD touchscreen runs iFIT; full content needs a paid membership. It folds on the SpaceSaver frame with EasyLift assist and measures 73.2 by 34.6 by 60.7 inches; the boxed weight is 249 lb. ProForm’s warranty is ten years on the frame, two years on the motor and other parts, one year on the touchscreen and one year of labour. Nebraska Furniture Mart listed it at $1,799 on 14 October 2026, and ProForm’s own site showed about $1,600 when we checked on 13 October.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Reviews", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/reviews/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "ProForm Carbon Pro 9000", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/proform-carbon-pro-9000-treadmill/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the difference between the ProForm Pro 9000 and the Carbon Pro 9000?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The older Pro 9000 had a 22-inch touchscreen, incline from -3% to 12% and a 300 lb rating. The current Carbon Pro 9000 (PFTL16925) has a 16-inch touchscreen, incline from 0 to 12% with no decline and a 350 lb rating. Both have a 20 by 60-inch belt.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the ProForm Carbon Pro 9000 treadmill worth it?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For walkers and moderate runners who will use iFIT on a big screen, it is a well-specified folding treadmill with a 350 lb rating. It is worth less if you will not keep a membership, and its motor warranty is two years. If you will not use the screen much, the Carbon Pro 2000 is better value. We have not tested it.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the weight limit on the ProForm Carbon Pro 9000?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "ProForm’s product sheet for PFTL16925 and Nebraska Furniture Mart’s listing both give 350 lb. The older Pro 9000 was rated to 300 lb.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does the ProForm Carbon Pro 9000 have decline?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No. The current Carbon Pro 9000 inclines from 0 to 12% with no decline. The older Pro 9000 declined to -3%, which is one way to tell them apart.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What motor does the ProForm Carbon Pro 9000 have?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "ProForm rates it at 3.6 CHP, and Treadmill Review Guru and T3 give the same figure. The motor is covered for two years. ProForm’s CHP figures are laboratory ratings that do not denote operational horsepower in household use.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How big is the ProForm Carbon Pro 9000 screen?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Sixteen inches. A listing or review describing a 22-inch screen is describing the older Pro 9000.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-10-14",
      dateModified: "2026-10-14",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.name.split(" ")[0] },
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 1,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/proform-carbon-pro-9000-treadmill/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-10-14",
    modifiedTime: "2026-10-14",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "proform carbon pro 9000 treadmill",
      "proform pro 9000 treadmill",
      "proform carbon pro 9000 review",
      "proform pro 9000 vs carbon pro 9000",
      "proform carbon pro 9000 specs",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "See the Verdict", link: "#who-should-buy" }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <svg class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full opacity-10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <pattern id="dot-pattern-proformcarbonpro9000treadmill" x="0" y="0" width="24" height="24" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <circle cx="2" cy="2" r="1.5" fill="white"></circle>
        </pattern>
        <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#dot-pattern-proformcarbonpro9000treadmill)"></rect>
      </svg>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-6 flex-wrap">
          <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Model Review
          </span>
          <span class="bg-green-500 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Updated October 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          ProForm Carbon Pro 9000 <span class="text-[#5AA9FF]">Treadmill Review</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          The Carbon Pro 9000 is the top of ProForm’s current treadmill range, and it shares a name with an older ProForm Pro 9000 that had a bigger screen, decline and a lower user rating. This review sets out what the current machine is, the figures ProForm and independent sources agree on, how to tell the two apart, and when a Carbon Pro 2000 or a NordicTrack is the better buy.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="#which-9000" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
            Pro 9000 vs Carbon Pro 9000
          </a>
          <a href="#who-should-buy" class="bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm border border-white/20">
            Who Should Buy It
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 py-8 border-b border-gray-100">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="48" height="48" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight"><a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author" class="text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a></p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">October 14, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="1.2k" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 m-0 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          14 October 2026 we read ProForm's syndicated product sheet for the Carbon Pro 9000 (SKU PFTL16925)
          and Nebraska Furniture Mart's listing for the same model number, which agree on the 16 in. HD
          touchscreen, 0-12 mph, 0-12% incline, the 350 lb maximum user weight and the 73.2 x 34.6 x 60.7 in.
          dimensions. proform.com blocked our automated check that day, so the 3.6 CHP motor rating and the
          20 x 60 in. belt rest on ProForm's own product page as we read it on 13 October 2026 for our
          <a href="/best-proform-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">ProForm roundup</a>,
          together with Treadmill Review Guru's review (updated January 2025) and T3's review, which give the
          same figures. Figures for the older Pro 9000 come from TreadmillReviews.com (updated October 2023)
          and Live Science, and are stated only where both agree. We have not tested either machine, and none
          of these numbers are our own measurements. Prices change constantly. We earn a commission if you buy
          through the Amazon link on this page; it does not change what we say about the machine.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-4">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-[#FF5A1F]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h7"></path></svg>
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">1. ProForm Carbon Pro 9000 Treadmill: The Short Answer</a>
          <a href="#which-9000" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">2. ProForm Pro 9000 vs Carbon Pro 9000: Two Different Machines</a>
          <a href="#current-specs" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">3. The Carbon Pro 9000 Specifications</a>
          <a href="#deck-and-motor" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">4. Deck, Motor and the 350 lb Rating</a>
          <a href="#incline-speed-screen" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">5. Incline, Speed and the 16-Inch Screen</a>
          <a href="#walking-or-running" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">6. Walking or Running: How the Specification Reads</a>
          <a href="#warranty-delivery" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">7. Warranty, Delivery and Returns</a>
          <a href="#space" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">8. Footprint, Folding and Ceiling Height</a>
          <a href="#what-reviewers-report" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">9. What Independent Reviewers Consistently Report</a>
          <a href="#vs-alternatives" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">10. Carbon Pro 9000 vs the Carbon Pro 2000 and NordicTrack</a>
          <a href="#buying" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">11. Buying Tips, Sales and Buying Used</a>
          <a href="#who-should-buy" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">12. Who Should Buy It, and Who Should Not</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">13. Frequently Asked Questions</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Search for the ProForm Pro 9000 treadmill and you will find two quite different machines. The
          one ProForm sells now is the Carbon Pro 9000, model PFTL16925: a 16-inch touchscreen, a 3.6 CHP
          motor rating, a 20 by 60-inch belt, incline to 12% with no decline, and a 350 lb rating. The one
          many older reviews describe is the earlier Pro 9000, with a 22-inch screen, decline to -3% and a
          300 lb rating. Both are real, both have been sold as ProForm's flagship, and their figures should
          not be mixed. This page is about the current machine, with a section on the older one for anyone
          buying used.
        </p>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">1. ProForm Carbon Pro 9000 Treadmill: The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>The ProForm Carbon Pro 9000 treadmill is the top of ProForm's current range: a 20 by
            60-inch folding deck, 0 to 12% incline, 12 mph, a 350 lb rating and a 16-inch touchscreen, with a
            motor ProForm rates at 3.6 CHP. It suits walkers and moderate runners who want iFIT on a big
            screen. It is not the older Pro 9000, which had a 22-inch screen and decline.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            Three facts carry most of the decision. The 350 lb rating is the highest in ProForm's range and
            higher than NordicTrack's T Series, which makes it a reasonable choice for heavier walkers. The
            incline stops at 0%: there is no decline, so iFIT's downhill route sections run flat. And the motor
            is covered for two years, which is short for a flagship; NordicTrack's Commercial 1750, at a higher
            price, covers its motor for life.
          </p>
          <p>
            Read every figure with the model number in mind. Reviews of the older Pro 9000 are still widely read,
            and its figures differ on the screen, the incline range and the capacity. We have not tested the
            Carbon Pro 9000; what follows is what ProForm's published figures and independent coverage imply.
            For the whole current ProForm range ranked, see our
            <a href="/best-proform-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best ProForm treadmills</a>
            roundup.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Product cards -->
      <div class="not-prose">
        {
          PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
              <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm">
                <div class="bg-gray-900 px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-3">
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="text-white font-black text-xl leading-tight m-0">
                      {index + 1}. {product.name}
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs">{product.category}</p>
                  </div>
                  <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
                    {product.badge}
                  </span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-6">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 flex-wrap">
                    <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400">Typical street price</span>
                    <span class="ml-auto font-black text-gray-900">{product.priceRange}</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-4">{product.specs}</p>
                  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6" set:html={product.description} />
                  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
                    <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-100 rounded-xl p-4">
                      <h4 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-green-700 mt-0 mb-2">What We Like</h4>
                      <ul class="space-y-2">
                        {product.pros.map((pro) => (
                          <li class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">{pro}</li>
                        ))}
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-xl p-4">
                      <h4 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-red-700 mt-0 mb-2">What We Don't Like</h4>
                      <ul class="space-y-2">
                        {product.cons.map((con) => (
                          <li class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">{con}</li>
                        ))}
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="border-t border-gray-100 pt-4">
                    <p class="text-gray-900 font-bold mb-4">{product.bottomLine}</p>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
                      <a href={product.amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
                        {product.amazonLabel} &rarr;
                      </a>
                      {product.reviewUrl && (
                        <a href={product.reviewUrl} class="text-[#0F62FE] font-bold no-underline text-sm hover:underline">
                          Read our full {product.name} review &rarr;
                        </a>
                      )}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <div id="which-9000" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">2. ProForm Pro 9000 vs Carbon Pro 9000: Two Different Machines</h2>
<p>
            ProForm has used the Pro 9000 name on more than one flagship treadmill. The one most older reviews
            describe, and the one many used listings are selling, is the generation before the Carbon Pro 9000.
            The differences are not cosmetic.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[480px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Specification</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Carbon Pro 9000 (current, PFTL16925)</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Older Pro 9000 (22 in. screen)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Screen</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">16 in. HD touchscreen</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">22 in. HD touchscreen</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Incline</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0 to 12%, no decline</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">-3% to 12%</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Belt</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">20 x 60 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">20 x 60 in.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Speed</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0-12 mph</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0-12 mph (one source)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Max user weight</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">350 lb</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">300 lb</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Motor rating</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">3.6 CHP</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">3.6 CHP (one source)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Boxed weight</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">249 lb</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">263 lb</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Warranty</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">10 yr frame; 2 yr motor and parts; 1 yr screen and labour</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">10 yr frame; 2 yr parts; 1 yr labour</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            The older column comes from TreadmillReviews.com's review, last updated in October 2023, and Live
            Science's review, which agree on the 22-inch screen, the -3% to 12% range, the 20 by 60-inch belt,
            the 300 lb rating, the 263 lb boxed weight and the warranty; the motor and speed figures appear in
            TreadmillReviews.com's specification list only. Treadmill Review Guru's review of the Carbon Pro 9000
            says in terms that the new machine does not decline like the previous Pro 9000 and has a higher
            weight capacity. Reviews of still-earlier ProForm machines sold under the Pro 9000 and SMART Pro 9000
            names describe smaller screens again, which is why screen sizes from 10 to 22 inches all turn up in
            search results for the same name.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">What changed, in practice</h3>
          <p>
            The Carbon Pro 9000 gave up the bigger screen and the decline, and gained 50 lb of rated capacity. For
            most buyers that is a fair trade. Decline is used less than incline by most owners, and a 16-inch
            screen is plenty to follow a class from a moving belt. For a runner training for hilly races, or
            anyone who wanted the largest screen available at the price, the older machine had features the
            current one does not.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">How to tell which one you are looking at</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Look at the screen.</strong> A 22-inch screen is the older Pro 9000. The current Carbon Pro 9000's is 16 inches.</li>
            <li><strong>Check the incline range.</strong> A listing that mentions -3% decline describes the older machine.</li>
            <li><strong>Read the model number.</strong> PFTL16925 is the current US Carbon Pro 9000. On a used machine, read it from the frame label.</li>
            <li><strong>Check the capacity.</strong> 350 lb is the current figure; 300 lb belongs to the older machine.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

