        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a Pro 9000</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Most bad Pro 9000 purchases come from reading the wrong generation’s figures.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Reading an old review as if it described the current machine</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Reviews of the 22-inch Pro 9000 describe decline and a 300 lb limit. The Carbon Pro 9000 has neither the decline nor the lower limit. Check the screen size and the model number.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying for the 9000’s screen and not using it</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The main thing the 9000 adds over the Carbon Pro 2000 is six inches of screen. If you will mostly walk to your own content, the Pro 2000 does the same job on the belt for less.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting flagship warranty terms</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The motor and parts are covered for two years, and the screen and labour for one. Plan for that, or price an extended plan before you buy.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying for downhill training</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The current Carbon Pro 9000 does not decline. If downhill running matters, the older Pro 9000 or a NordicTrack Commercial model does.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

